  "configuration_id": "config_022",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_016 (multimodal, PCA n2000 + ResNet50, concat) achieves 0.527 acc, outperforming RNA alone (0.485) and image alone (0.208). The image modality contributes ~4% in combination but is very weak standalone, suggesting ResNet50 may be underfitting the image signal. Question tested: config_022 swaps only the image encoder to ImageNet-pretrained ViT-L while keeping everything else identical to config_016 (single profile, PCA n2000, concat fusion), giving a clean single-variable test of whether a stronger image encoder increases the multimodal gain. Why best next: If ViT-L substantially lifts accuracy, it confirms the image encoder is the bottleneck and justifies exploring multiprofile/aggregation variants with ViT-L (configs 024-027). If it does not, we learn the image modality has a hard ceiling and should focus budget on RNA encoder upgrades or fusion strategy. This single experiment resolves a high-uncertainty design choice that gates many downstream configurations, making it the most budget-efficient next step."
}

